{"id":1751512,"retrievedAt":"2026-08-18T11:51:50.448Z","response":{"adult":false,"backdrop_path":null,"belongs_to_collection":null,"budget":0,"genres":[{"id":99,"name":"Documentary"},{"id":36,"name":"History"}],"homepage":"","id":1751512,"imdb_id":null,"origin_country":["US"],"original_language":"en","original_title":"At The Wheel: A History of Driving and Driving Safety Film","overview":"This film from director/producer Rodney Jacobs and Freewheelin' Films,  \"At the Wheel / A History of Driving and Driving Safety Film\" (1980) explores the evolution of driving and the importance of skill behind the wheel. It begins with the invention of the automobile in the late 19th century. As roads improved and cars became faster, driving evolved into a challenging and exciting activity that demanded skill.  The film also traces the rise of safety awareness, particularly in response to increasing road fatalities in the 1960s, leading to innovations like seat belts and the growth of professional driving schools. The film concludes by affirming that while most people won’t race professionally, every driver can benefit from improving their skills for greater safety, confidence, and enjoyment on the road.","popularity":0.0071,"poster_path":null,"production_companies":[{"id":251628,"logo_path":null,"name":"Freewheelin' Films LTD","origin_country":""}],"production_countries":[{"iso_3166_1":"US","name":"United States of America"}],"release_date":"1980-01-01","revenue":0,"runtime":17,"softcore":false,"spoken_languages":[],"status":"Released","tagline":"","title":"At The Wheel: A History of Driving and Driving Safety Film","video":false,"vote_average":0,"vote_count":0,"alternative_titles":{"titles":[]},"credits":{"cast":[{"adult":false,"gender":2,"id":4787723,"known_for_department":"Acting","name":"Sam Posey","original_name":"Sam Posey","popularity":0.3144,"profile_path":"/dC4W03aCxs8umNqhWhdTzsfBmO5.jpg","cast_id":3,"character":"Host / Narrator","credit_id":"6a83697938cbd4ce01a97500",